---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import ArticleSchema from '../../components/ArticleSchema.astro';
import { site, description, pageTitle } from '../../content';

const path = '/use-cases/segmentation';
const title = pageTitle(site, 'use-cases/segmentation');
const desc = description(site, 'use-cases/segmentation');
---

<BaseLayout title={title} description={desc} site={site} path={path}>
  <ArticleSchema title={title} description={desc} siteName={site.name} domain={site.domain} path={path} />
  <section class="container py-16">
    <a href="/use-cases" class="link text-sm font-bold">← All use cases</a>
    <h1 class="hero-title mt-5">Design actionable Shopify customer segments</h1>
    <p class="mt-7 max-w-3xl text-xl leading-9 text-slate-700">A segment is an operational decision about who receives a particular message, supported by a reproducible membership rule.</p>
    <article class="prose-shopify card mt-12 max-w-4xl p-8">
      <h2>Write the rule before the name</h2>
      <p>Specify the action, source fields, observation window and refresh requirement. Distinguish unknown data from a confirmed negative: no recorded order may reflect a profile merge problem. Keep a versioned definition so a later analyst can explain why someone qualified at send time.</p>
      <h2>Define priority and exit behavior</h2>
      <p>Map collisions among welcome, cart, browse and retention audiences. Decide which message takes priority, whether the lower-priority flow waits or exits, and how long the decision remains relevant. Membership in an eligible segment does not itself establish permission to use a channel.</p>
      <h2>Treat late data explicitly</h2>
      <p>Choose what happens when a purchase arrives after a customer was queued, or a refund changes lifetime spend. Recheck critical exclusions before send where the system supports it. If updates are delayed, document that limitation and choose a workflow that can tolerate it rather than claiming real-time behavior.</p>
      <h2>Evaluate reproducibility and portability</h2>
      <p>Request a dated membership export and the rule that produced it. Ask how identities merge, time zones are interpreted and exclusions propagate between tools. Compare a small set of explained customer histories before adding predictive scores; an opaque score cannot replace a defined campaign action.</p>
      <h2>Proposed boundary exercise</h2>
      <p>Create staff profiles just inside and outside each declared condition, including missing dates and reversed purchases. Replay a late event and inspect both enrollment and exit. Monitor unexplained membership changes and message overlap. Segment size alone says nothing about usefulness or incremental revenue.</p>
    </article>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
